Subject: openssl: refuse "" and directory paths before BIO_new_file on OpenVMS

The OpenVMS C RTL opens "" for writing (it creates a file named ".") and
a directory path as a file beside the directory ("tests." next to
TESTS.DIR), where glibc fails with ENOENT and EISDIR (vms-php probe
r_fopen_odd).  openssl_cms_sign(), openssl_pkcs7_sign/encrypt/decrypt()
and openssl_pkcs12_export_to_file() then "succeeded" on such paths and
left those files behind (7 openssl tests, vms-php PORTING_LOG #32).  On
VMS php_openssl_bio_new_file() fails for them, as BIO_new_file does on
other systems.
---
--- a/ext/openssl/openssl_backend_common.c
+++ b/ext/openssl/openssl_backend_common.c
@@ -1623,6 +1623,17 @@
 		return NULL;
 	}
 
+#ifdef __VMS
+	/* The C RTL opens "" for writing (a file named ".") and a directory path
+	 * as a file beside the directory ("tests." next to TESTS.DIR), where
+	 * glibc fails with ENOENT and EISDIR. */
+	{
+		zend_stat_t sb;
+		if (file_path[0] == '\0' || (VCWD_STAT(file_path, &sb) == 0 && S_ISDIR(sb.st_mode))) {
+			return NULL;
+		}
+	}
+#endif
 	bio = BIO_new_file(file_path, mode);
 	if (bio == NULL) {
 		php_openssl_store_errors();
